{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792443268,"nonce":"01tK/7Vw2r9ZoENAGz3UHhWGpr0=","message":"Implemented in 57e9971098b96768fef49141f5d6b8232f20b87c, local, not pushed.\n\nKind 32 fill 3 now retains the producer's fit, free-space position fractions, pixel offsets and repeat bits rather than reporting a valid mapping as unsupported. ImageDraw and the record reader moved into display_list/image.rs, with ImageDraw re-exported from plan for existing imports. ImageMapping now reports invalid metadata or intrinsic geometry. ImageResource supplies a texture, intrinsic logical size, legacy fit and mask mode through Painter::render_with_images. Painter::render still accepts the existing GpuImage resolver; it defaults to the texture's dimensions, ordinary stretching and colour sampling. SDK slot encodings remain caller-owned. Explicit record mappings override the resource's legacy fit. Invalid resources are skipped and returned with missing image slots.\n\nCover, contain, fill, tile, none and scale-down resolve at draw time without moving the content quad or its clips. The logical mapping rectangle is scaled into the quad's normalized affine frame; separate auxiliary rows hold its rectangle, repeat axes and analytic AA width. They follow existing clip/shape data without rebasing shape pointers. Repeat uses fract for negative coordinates and clamps sampling half a texel inside each cell. Nonrepeated axes retain antialiased rectangle coverage. Masks ignore texture RGB and use the record's tint and alpha exactly once. Background image brush records use the same path, including brush opacity, shape clips and enclosing layers. The existing abi_clip vec4 carries the clip pointer in X, mask flag in Y and mapping pointer in Z. GpuImageInstance remains 13 vec4, 208 bytes; GpuPrimitive remains 34 vec4, 544 bytes. Native zero metadata keeps its previous rendering. No additional render target or resampled texture is allocated. Ordinary stretched images borrow their existing auxiliary rows; resolved mappings append two rows to a temporary vector.\n\nThe reference is ashui's Images.hx positioned mapping and ImageShader.hx sampling contract, with existing Blinc clip AA preserved. Nineteen producer scenes at display scales 1 and 2 generate 38 fixtures. generate_mappings.py copies blinc_abi a92f5c0 into a scratch directory, adds two probe-only context accessors for mapping state unavailable through the public owned-context API, and runs its unchanged display-list encoder with generate_mappings.rs. The actual ABI checkout, encoder, schema, shared ClipPath and CSS types remain unchanged. The generator, scratch adapter and fixtures are committed together.\n\nOn Apple M1 Pro, Metal, 58 render cases stay within 1/255 in every RGBA channel against an independent CPU oracle reading raw encoder rows, bilinear texture pixels and intrinsic resource metadata. No probes are skipped. Cases cover all six fits, fractional positions and offsets, both shrink and no-enlarge scale-down branches, differing intrinsic and texture sizes, negative tile coordinates, no-repeat/X/Y/both repeats, masks with tint alpha and inherited opacity, affine mapping with rounded/faded/ellipse clipping, consecutive overlapping mapped images, nested filtered layers, mapped background brushes and legacy resource-selected fits. The same Painter is reused. All 28 display-list GPU tests and the polygon fill-rule test pass with normal capabilities. All 28 display-list tests also pass with vertex storage disabled. With both storage flags disabled and primitive/glyph capacities 1024, all 58 mapping cases pass on Metal. This checks the image data-texture path, not the stale SDF packing tracked by ce34b20. Actual WebGL2, PowerVR/Adreno compilation and mobile pixels remain unverified.\n\nMutations: dropping position fails by 178/255; dropping logical-to-device mapping scale fails by 205/255 at display scale 2; disabling horizontal repetition fails by 155/255; and treating masks as tinted colour textures fails by 71/255. All temporary mutations and capability overrides were restored.\n\nGate: fmt, workspace clippy with no new warnings, 1,906 workspace nextest tests passed (54 skipped), docs with warnings denied, wasm and iOS compile checks, and threaded layout/CN tests pass. All 98 GPU-free integration tests, four image geometry/mask/shader unit tests and the image resource API doctest pass. Both composed image shader variants validate under Naga. The separate DSL run has 516 passed, 28 failed, 10 skipped, with exactly the same 28 failing names as the untouched ff83adca baseline under a33d2b9. No dependency sources changed.","files":null}]}